From: Mansur Aliyu <mansurmasama@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:00:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Single selfish-mining attacker, transaction batching,
 stricter pilot checks

Prepared with Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) and tested on pilot rows.

Single attacker (manuscript change agreed with Niclas):
- New manifest column adversarial_hashing_power_share (alpha, in [0, 0.25]);
  number_of_attackers is 1 if alpha > 0, else 0.
- The attacker holds exactly alpha of the total hashing power; honest nodes keep
  their Dirichlet draw for H_hash, rescaled to 1 - alpha (same random stream).
- Rows with the old fraction_of_attackers column behave exactly as before.
  Previously the attackers' combined share was not controlled (0.00002 to 0.83
  in the pilot), which produced majority takeovers and runs without rounds.

Transaction batching (computational feasibility):
- New manifest column transaction_batch_size (b, default 1). One simulated
  transaction stands for b transactions: b * S_tx bytes at rate lambda_tx / b.
  Block filling and bandwidth use are unchanged; TPS is multiplied by b; TCR and
  CL are unchanged. b is the smallest of 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100 that keeps the
  expected (node, transaction) entries of a run below 1e8; b = 1 for 66% of
  primary rows. The audit records transactionBatchSize.

Sampling and manifests:
- two_level_nested_lhs_monte_carlo.py exports adversarial_hashing_power_share
  (same LHS values as the former f_A) and transaction_batch_size.
- generate_execution_manifests.py requires both columns. Run IDs and seeds are
  unchanged.

verify_pilot_results.py:
- FAILs on incomplete runs (unless --allow-incomplete), complete runs with zero
  TPS or no window transactions, a realized attacker share or batch size that
  differs from the manifest; warns on reorganized windows and SBR > 0.5;
  prints termination reasons.

